liveAlerts = input.bool(false, "Master: enable notifications", group="5. Alerts", display=display.none, tooltip="Off by default. Enable this and the required notification switches, then create a TradingView alert using Any alert() function call. Direction and non-SL exits use closed bars; SL can notify intrabar. Notifications only: no broker orders, account permissions or fills.")

// ── 6. Reference display and episode reset ──────────────────────────────────
signalRearmBars = input.int(2, "Signal episode: structural reset closes", minval=1, maxval=5, group="1. Decision", display=display.none, tooltip="Re-arm only after the selected number of complete known closes BOTH lose the episode MOM direction and cross to the opposite EMA side. Failed breakout, no-chase, Delta or ADX alone never re-arm. Missing data breaks reset counting but preserves the episode. Opposite qualified direction starts its own episode.")
showExitRow = input.bool(true, "Show SL / TP / Exit row", group="4. Display", display=display.none)
showTP3Trend = input.bool(true, "Show TREND CONT after confirmed TP3", group="4. Display", display=display.none, tooltip="Display only, after a completed TP3 touch. Latest completed own-chart MOM3/MOM6, active EMA side, normalized DI spread and the own-ADX enter/hold state must still support the original reference direction. No new-entry breakout, no-chase, estimated Delta or Overall Trend veto. Loss of alignment removes the tag; a later aligned close may restore it while the same post-TP3 path is intact. A gap, structural reset, session end or later touch of the original SL ends this context monitor. TP3 remains final: no new target, entry, stop order, actual position tracking or prediction.")
manualMaxHoldBars = input.int(6, "Manual time exit: chart durations (0=off)", minval=0, maxval=100, group="7. Manual position", display=display.none)
